me    | Type     | Description                                              |\n| ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | What the agent is browsing for, like \"Pricing research\". |"],[83,"| Name    | Type     | Description                                             |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `limit` | `number` | The size of the context window, in tokens, like 200000. |"],[198,"| Name    | Type     | Description                                        |\n| ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `label` | `string` | What the agent is doing, in a few words. Required. |"],[8,"| Name    | Type     | Description                                    |\n| ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The header text. Defaults to \"Agent activity\". |"],[279,"| Name    | Type     | Description                                 |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The run's name, shown over the status line. |"],[100,"| Name    | Type     | Description                               |\n| ------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The run's name, like \"Indexing the docs\". |"],[156,"| Name    | Type     | Description                            |\n| ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The queue's name over its status line. |"],[144,"| Name    | Type     | Description                 |\n| ------- | -------- | --------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | Defaults to \"Credits used\". |"],[35,"| Name   | Type                                                                                                                      | Description                                        |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tone` | `neutral \\| accent \\| success \\| warning \\| danger \\| blue \\| violet \\| green \\| orange \\| red \\| yellow \\| pink \\| teal` | Color as text on its own tint. Neutral by default. |"],[124,"| Name   | Type                                | Description                                                          |\n| ------ | ----------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `view` | `plan \\| notes \\| sources \\| edits` | Which part to show. Leave it out to start on the first one there is. |"],[201,"| Name   | Type                              | Description                  |\n| ------ | --------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `file` | `{ name: string; type?: string }` | A file chip after the label. |"],[26,"| Name   | Type                    | Description                                                     |\n| ------ | ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `took` | `Record<phase, number>` | Seconds each phase took, for the list a finished line opens to. |"],[66,"| Name   | Type             | Description                           |\n| ------ | ---------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `size` | `sm \\| md \\| lg` | The three sizes; `md` is the default. |"],[142,"| Name   | Type           | Description                                                        |\n| ------ | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `rows` | `RunCostRow[]` | The breakdown under the bar; each row has a `label` and a `value`. |"],[120,"| Name   | Type         | Description                                                                                  |\n| ------ | ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `plan` | `PlanStep[]` | The plan. Each step has a `label`, an optional `detail`, and a `state` of done, now or next. |"],[267,"| Name   | Type        | Description                     |\n| ------ | ----------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `note` | `ReactNode` | A quiet line under the toolbar. |"],[155,"| Name   | Type       | Description                                                                                                               |\n| ------ | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `jobs` | `RunJob[]` | The jobs in the queue. Each has a title, an agent, an icon, a state, an optional progress, a time, a note, and its steps. |"],[36,"| Name   | Type       | Description                                    |\n| ------ | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `size` | `sm \\| md` | `sm` is 20px tall, `md` is 24px (the default). |"],[38,"| Name   | Type       | Description               |\n| ------ | ---------- | ------------------------- |\n| `icon` | `IconName` | An icon before the label. |"],[67,"| Name   | Type       | Description               |\n| ------ | ---------- | ------------------------- |\n| `icon` | `IconName` | An icon before the label. |"],[11,"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                       |\n| ------ | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread (the default). Set false to give it a card of its own. |"],[126,"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                       |\n| ------ | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread (the default). Set false to give it a card of its own. |"],[145,"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                       |\n| ------ | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread (the default). Set false to give it a card of its own. |"],[296,"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                    |\n| ------ | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `done` | `boolean` | True once searching and reading are over. The trail folds to its summary line. |"],[298,"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                           |\n| ------ | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `open` | `boolean` | Whether the trail is open. Left out, it folds once `done` turns true. |"],[125,"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                          |\n| ------ | --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `open` | `boolean` | Whether the trail is open. Leave it out to let the header toggle it. |"],[89,"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                        |\n| ------ | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `open` | `boolean` | Whether the panel is open. Leave it out to let the pill toggle it. |"],[162,"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                 |\n| ------ | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread, with no card. False by default. |"],[300,"| Name   | Type      | Description                                            |\n| ------ | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Without the panel, for a chat stream. True by default. |"],[281,"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                                                                                                   |\n| ------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `time` | `number` | Seconds into the run while it streams in. Spans that start later stay hidden, running ones reach this far. Leave it out once the run is over. |"],[200,"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                                                |\n| ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `meta` | `string` | Quiet detail after the label, like \"2 of 4\". Changing only this does not restart the pill. |"],[282,"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                                               |\n| ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `axis` | `number` | Seconds the time axis covers. Defaults to the run's length, rounded up to a whole second. |"],[24,"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                                       |\n| ------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `slow` | `object` | Shown while the phase takes long, with Stop. Has `text` and an optional `onStop`. |"],[88,"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                             |\n| ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hint` | `string` | The quiet line beside the button. Defaults to \"Summarises older turns\". |"],[103,"| Name   | Type     | Description                 |\n| ------ | -------- | --------------------------- |\n| `step` | `number` | The step in hand, from `0`. |"],[136,"| Name   | Type     | Description          |\n| ------ | -------- | -------------------- |\n| `used` | `number` | Credits used so far. |"],[37,"| Name  | Type      | Description                                  |\n| ----- | --------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `dot` | `boolean` | A dot in the badge's color before the label. |"],[25,"| Name  | Type     | Description                                                                                                               |\n| ----- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ask` | `object` | What the agent waits for in the waiting phase. Has `text`, optional `approveLabel`, `onApprove` and optional `onDecline`. |"],[52,"| Name  | Type     | Description                                                                            |\n| ----- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ask` | `object` | While a step waits: the button that lets the agent go on. Has a `label` and `onAllow`. |"],[48,"| Name  | Type     | Description                                                     |\n| ----- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `url` | `string` | The address bar: the page's address, or the search being typed. |"],[175,"| Name | Type            | Description                                                                    |\n| ---- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `as` | `tabs \\| radio` | `tabs` (the default) when it switches a panel, `radio` when it sets an option. |"],[176,"| Name | Type     | Description                                                                                                                                        |\n| ---- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id` | `string` | Ties the tabs to their panel: give the panel an id of the form \"id-panel\" and point its aria-labelledby at \"id-value\". Defaults to a generated id. |"],[109,"A `ProgressMeter` is `{ label, value, max, unit?, warnAt?, dangerAt?, dangerLabel?, note? }`: it\nreads \"On track\" until `value / max` crosses `warnAt` (\"Running low\") and then `dangerAt` (the\n`dangerLabel`, or \"Almost out\")."],[163,"A `RunJob` state is queued, running, failed, or done. A `RunStep` has a label, a state, and an\noptional meta shown once the step is done. Progress defaults to the share of a job's steps that are\ndone."],[287,"A `TraceSpan` has an `id`, a `name`, a `kind` (agent, llm, tool, or retrieval), a `start` and\n`duration` in seconds, optional `tokens`, optional `input` and `output` strings, and optional\n`children`. An agent span without its own token count adds up every span under it."],[301,"A `WebPage` has a `title`, a `domain`, an optional `date`, a `status` (reading, read, skimmed,\npaywall, blocked, or timeout), and an optional `cite` number the answer refers to it by."],[34,"A badge is a compact label. Its `tone` picks the color (neutral, the accent tint, the three\nstates, or one of eight tag colors). Two sizes, an optional dot or icon before the label, and an\noptional remove button after it."],[46,"A browser session shows the agent browsing the web for you: a small browser frame with the page it\nis on, the steps it takes under it, and Pause and Take over. When a step waits for you — a cookie\nbanner in the way, say — it shows why and a button to let the agent go on. Take over hands the page\nto you: its frame turns the accent colour, its controls become usable, and the button reads Hand\nback."],[64,"A button is a pill in one of the variants — `primary` for the main action, `soft` and `line` for the\nrest, `ghost` for the quietest — in three sizes. Return a promise from `onClick` and the button runs\nitself: it shows the busy face until the promise settles, then the done face. `ButtonCopy` copies\ntext and flashes a check."],[81,"A context meter is a pill with a ring that shows how full the context window is. It opens a panel\nwith one bar split by kind, a legend whose rows list what is in each part, and a Compact button\nthat summarises older turns to free room. The ring turns orange past a warning share, and a message\nline fades in with a warning or a result."],[207,"A named-steps progress list with a loader beside the running step, a track that fills as steps finish, and an expandable list of every step."],[60,"A pill button in the library's variants and sizes, with built-in busy, done and pressed states."],[150,"A queue of agent jobs in three parts — the one running with its steps and progress, the ones up next, and the ones done — with a compact toggle."],[116,"A reasoning trail is the structured record the agent leaves after it thinks: a plan it works\nthrough, the notes it took, the sources it read, or the edits it made. Pick what it shows with\n`view`. The header counts the seconds and shimmers while the run is live, folds the trail away, and\nsettles on \"Reasoned for Ns\" once it finishes."],[179,"A row of KPIs, each with its change against the period before and a sparkline, with a period switch that rolls the numbers and redraws the lines."],[135,"A run cost shows the credits a run has used against its budget, as a number and a meter. A cap\nmarks where the agent pauses, drawn as a line across the bar; when the spend reaches it the status\nturns amber and the run pauses. The breakdown under the bar shows the tokens and tool calls behind\nthe number, and the button starts, stops, resumes or raises the cap by status."],[154,"A run queue shows a batch of agent jobs moving through three parts. The job running is raised on\nits own card with its agent, its steps, a progress bar and the time left. The jobs up next wait\nbelow, each with when it should start, and the jobs done sit under them with how long each took and\na green tick. A failed step turns its job red and offers a Retry; a Detailed / Compact switch folds\nthe running job's steps away; and once every job is done a summary takes the running job's place."],[95,"A run's progress three ways — a ring for the whole run, segments for its steps and a bar for the step in hand — with controls and an optional meter that warns as it fills."],[170,"A segmented control picks one of a few options. A white knob slides to the picked one. As `tabs`\n(the default) it switches a panel; as a `radio` group it sets an option. The arrow keys move along\nand pick, and Home and End jump to the ends. The `label` is required and names the group for screen\nreaders."],[30,"A small label for a plan, environment, or status, with an optional dot or icon and an optional remove button."],[197,"A status pill shows a single line of what the agent is up to. Its `state` picks the glyph and\ncolour — `thinking`, `reading` and `working` shimmer while they run — and a new `state`, `label`,\n`file` or `action` fades the old line out before the new one arrives. The `bar` variant is taller\nand draws a `progress` track along its bottom."],[211,"A step loader shows an agent's work as named steps. The step running now sits beside a small\nloader; a track below fills as steps finish; and the row expands to the full list, each line\nswitching to its `done` text once complete. When `current` reaches the number of steps, every step\nis done and the row shows the `doneLabel`."],[224,"A thinking state is a small animated mark beside a status line. Pick one of six marks with\n`variant`; give it `steps` and, with more than one, they take turns every `interval` unless you\ndrive the index with `current`. An elapsed-seconds counter sits at the end of the line and counts\nby itself unless you set `seconds` or hide it with `seconds={false}`."],[236,"A thinking trace is the reasoning log an agent writes as it works. Each step arrives on a line that\nspins while it runs and turns into a green check once it finishes, with what it found written under\nit and how long it took at its right. The header counts seconds while it runs; once the last step\nlands it becomes a summary of the work and the trace folds itself away."],[250,"A toast is a short message on a surface. Its `tone` picks the icon and colour — `loading` spins —\nand it takes a `title`, an optional `description` and an optional `action` button. Pass a new `id`\nto slide a new toast in and the old one away; keep the same `id` to change the text in place."],[271,"A tool's `tip` overrides its `label` in the tooltip, so set it only when the tip should say more\nthan the button's name; the `kbd` shortcut is shown after it. A person's `working: true` swaps the\ngreen status dot for the agent's thinking dots."],[260,"A toolbar whose labels wait a moment, then follow the pointer instantly between buttons, with a richer hover card for people."],[264,"A tooltip is the label that waits a moment under a toolbar button, then follows the pointer\ninstantly as it moves between them. Buttons come in `groups` with a line between, each with a `tip`\nand an optional shortcut (`kbd`). Avatars at the end get a richer card instead — a person's name,\nrole and what they are doing now, with an agent shown by its thinking dots."],[278,"A trace view lays one agent run out as a waterfall. Every span — an LLM call, a tool call, a\nretrieval, a sub-agent — sits on a shared time axis, nested under the span that started it with a\ntree's guides. Each kind has its own colour, counted in the key. While the run streams, a playhead\nmarks now and running bars glow at their leading edge; a tool call that runs over its budget turns\namber and hatched and is tagged slow. Open any span to see where it sat in the run, its input, its\noutput, its latency and its tokens."],[1,"Action log"],[14,"Agent phases"],[19,"Agent phases show which phase the agent is in, in one line: its glyph, its name shimmering while the\nphase lasts, and the seconds so far, with a track of six short segments under it that fills phase by\nphase. When the agent needs you, is slow or fails, a line under the track says so with what to do;\nonce it is done the line reads how long it took and opens to the phases it ran through."],[6,"An action log is a streaming list of what the agent does: each read, search, edit or command\nlands as a row, running with a spinner, then done with a check and the time it took. A row with\noutput opens to show it, like a diff or test run. The header shows a spinner while the run is live\nand a green dot once it finishes."],[29,"Badge"],[41,"Browser session"],[59,"Buttons"],[320,"Components are grouped by what they do in an agent product:"],[76,"Context meter"],[319,"Design tokens (`--dm-*` on the web, `DmColors`/`DmSpace`/`DmRadius` in Flutter) drive every color,\nspace, radius, and motion — change a token once and it flows everywhere."],[190,"Each `StatCardsStat` carries `values: { value, change, points }[]` — one entry per period, in the\nsame order as `periods` — where `value` is the number, `change` is the percent against the period\nbefore, and `points` is the sparkline oldest first."],[310,"Each component in these docs has a **live preview** you can toggle between light/dark and the two\nstyles, plus the code for all four frameworks side by side."],[316,"Every component responds to the same two switches, so your whole UI changes at once:"],[2,"Every tool call the agent makes, as a list that grows while it works, where each row opens to show its output."],[305,"Four frameworks, one design"],[308,"Get started"],[77,"How full the context is and what fills it, with a Compact action to free room."],[303,"Introduction"],[131,"Live credit and token spend against a budget, with a cap the agent pauses at."],[304,"Native UI components for AI-agent products, in four frameworks."],[274,"One agent run as an observability waterfall — every span on a shared time axis, nested under the span that started it, with its tokens and latency."],[166,"One choice from a few views or options, with a white knob that slides to the picked one. Works as tabs or as a radio group, fully keyboard driven."],[15,"One line for which phase an agent is in, from thinking to done, that stops to ask, says when it is slow, and folds to how long it took."],[193,"One live line for what an agent is doing right now, fading between its states and resizing to fit them."],[246,"One toast at a time — a new one rises in while the last one slips away."],[327,"Pick a component from the sidebar, copy the snippet for your framework, and drop it in. Pull the\nshared core once (tokens + helpers), and every component you add just works."],[94,"Progress"],[99,"Progress shows a long run three ways at once: a ring for the whole run, a segment per step, and a\nbar for how far the step in hand has got. The `state` colours it — grey while indeterminate or\npaused, the accent while running, red with a Retry on error, green when complete — and the controls\nfollow (Pause, Resume, Run again). An optional `meter` underneath warns in words as it fills."],[4,"Properties"],[17,"Properties"],[32,"Properties"],[44,"Properties"],[62,"Properties"],[79,"Properties"],[97,"Properties"],[114,"Properties"],[133,"Properties"],[152,"Properties"],[168,"Properties"],[181,"Properties"],[195,"Properties"],[209,"Properties"],[222,"Properties"],[234,"Properties"],[248,"Properties"],[262,"Properties"],[276,"Properties"],[292,"Properties"],[111,"Reasoning trail"],[130,"Run cost"],[149,"Run queue"],[307,"Sections"],[165,"Segmented Control"],[220,"Six animated indicators, each a small mark beside a status line that steps through what an agent is doing, with an optional elapsed-seconds counter."],[178,"Stat cards"],[183,"Stat cards are a row of numbers that matter. Each card has an icon, a label, the value in large\ntype, its change against the period before (green from zero, red below), and a sparkline in its own\ncolour. A `period` switch along the top rolls the numbers to their new values and redraws every\nline."],[192,"Status pill"],[206,"Step Loader"],[42,"The agent browsing the web for you step by step, in a small browser frame with the steps it takes, and Pause and Take over."],[112,"The agent's plan, notes, sources or edits, under a header it can fold away."],[290,"The agent's web searches as a trail — each query and what came back, each page read, skimmed or skipped and why, and an answer whose citations light their pages."],[232,"The live trace an agent writes as it works, each step turning green as it finishes, then folded away into a summary."],[315,"The Vanilla and React versions are the reference; Angular and Flutter are native ports that mirror\nthe same props and behavior."],[5,"Theming"],[18,"Theming"],[33,"Theming"],[45,"Theming"],[63,"Theming"],[80,"Theming"],[98,"Theming"],[115,"Theming"],[134,"Theming"],[153,"Theming"],[169,"Theming"],[182,"Theming"],[196,"Theming"],[210,"Theming"],[223,"Theming"],[235,"Theming"],[249,"Theming"],[263,"Theming"],[277,"Theming"],[293,"Theming"],[306,"Theming"],[231,"Thinking"],[219,"Thinking States"],[245,"Toast"],[259,"Tooltip"],[273,"Trace view"],[3,"Usage"],[16,"Usage"],[31,"Usage"],[43,"Usage"],[61,"Usage"],[78,"Usage"],[96,"Usage"],[113,"Usage"],[132,"Usage"],[151,"Usage"],[167,"Usage"],[180,"Usage"],[194,"Usage"],[208,"Usage"],[221,"Usage"],[233,"Usage"],[247,"Usage"],[261,"Usage"],[275,"Usage"],[291,"Usage"],[289,"Web search"],[294,"Web search shows an agent researching out loud. Each query is a row with how many results came\nback and how long it took; a query that finds nothing is asked again in other words. Under each\nquery sit the pages it opened, each marked Read, Skimmed, or Skipped with the reason (paywall,\nblocked, timeout). Once the run is done the trail folds to one line and the answer streams in,\nits bracketed numbers pointing back at the pages that back them up."],[40,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the badge is squared off and set in small caps with a hairline in its own color; in Soft\nit is a pill."],[272,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the bar and card are squared off with hairline borders; in Soft they are rounded panels.\nThe tooltip itself and the avatar colours (`--dm-av-*`) come from the theme, so they stay legible on\neither background."],[148,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the bar, the tag and the toggle are squared off; in Soft they are rounded. The fill takes\nthe accent mark while running and the warning mark once paused at the cap, and the status tag tints\nto match its state, all from the tokens."],[288,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the bars square off and running bars switch from a sweeping sheen to a steady stripe. Each\nkind keeps its colour from the chart palette; a slow bar is amber and hatched in every theme."],[191,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the cards are squared off with hairline borders; in Soft they are rounded panels with a\nsofter shadow. The sparkline colours fall back to the chart palette (the accent, then violet, green\nand orange) unless a card sets its own `color`."],[129,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the header, chips and edit blocks are squared off with hairline edges; in Soft they are\nrounded. The timeline rail, the pulse on the current step, and the shimmer on the title all take\ntheir colors from the tokens; added and removed lines use the add and remove colors."],[93,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the pill, the bar and the panel are squared off; in Soft they are rounded. The ring takes\nthe accent mark and the warning mark past the warning share, and the bar segments take the part\npalette (blue, teal, violet, grey) from the tokens unless a part sets its own color."],[110,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the ring, segments and bar are squared off with hairline tracks; in Soft they are rounded\nwith a softer fill. The state colours and the meter's warn and danger bands come from the theme, so\nthey read correctly on either background."],[13,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the rows and the output panes are squared off with hairline edges; in Soft they are\nrounded chips with soft fills. Added and removed lines in a row's output take the add and remove\ncolors from the tokens."],[164,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the running job gets a hairline in the accent and the progress bars fill in steps. A\nfailed job turns red with a hatched fill; the step glyphs are a spinner while running, a tick when\ndone, and a cross on failure."],[302,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). Skipped\npages dim and their tag turns amber; a running page shows a spinner. The site initials stack on the\nheader, and hovering a citation lights the page that backs it up along with its site mark."],[230,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\nmarks and the typed line use the active theme's accent and text colors; the counter is set in the\nnumeric style. Motion is paused for readers who prefer reduced motion — the line is shown whole\nrather than typed."],[244,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\nrunning step turns in the accent with a soft halo, finished steps and the rail between them turn\ngreen, and a slow step waits in amber. In Blueprint the marks are squared off and the result writes\nin with a plain fade instead of a blur."],[218,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\ntrack and loader take the accent color from the active theme; in Soft the row and track are softer\nand more rounded than in Blueprint."],[177,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\ntrack and sliding knob take the active theme's surface and accent colors; in Blueprint the control\nis squared off, in Soft it is a pill with a rounder knob."],[75,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\nvariants read against the theme's accent and surface tokens; in Soft the pills are rounder and\nsofter, and the busy and done faces blur across in either theme."],[258,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface with the toast shadow and its tone tints come from the theme tokens, so it reads\nagainst the dark stage; in Soft the card and its buttons are rounder."],[28,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The glyph\nand the current segment take the phase's colour — the accent while it works, amber while it waits,\nred on an error and green when done. In Blueprint the segments are squared off and the shimmer rests\non a solid colour."],[58,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The page\nis drawn small, with real words where they matter and grey lines for the rest; a price the agent has\ntaken is marked in the accent fill. While you have control the frame turns the accent colour. In\nBlueprint the frame and chips are squared off."],[205,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The pill\nsits on a surface with the shared shadow, so it picks up the theme's surface and token colours; in\nSoft it is rounder, and in dark it reads against the dark stage."]],"type":"string"},"page_id":{"docs":{"1":25,"2":26,"3":27,"4":28,"5":29,"6":30,"7":31,"8":32,"9":33,"10":34,"11":35,"12":36,"13":37,"14":38,"15":39,"16":40,"17":41,"18":42,"19":43,"20":44,"21":45,"22":46,"23":47,"24":48,"25":49,"26":50,"27":51,"28":52,"29":53,"30":54,"31":55,"32":56,"33":57,"34":58,"35":59,"36":60,"37":61,"38":62,"39":63,"40":64,"41":65,"42":66,"43":67,"44":68,"45":69,"46":70,"47":71,"48":72,"49":73,"50":74,"51":75,"52":76,"53":77,"54":78,"55":79,"56":80,"57":81,"58":82,"59":83,"60":84,"61":85,"62":86,"63":87,"64":88,"65":89,"66":90,"67":91,"68":92,"69":93,"70":94,"71":95,"72":96,"73":97,"74":98,"75":99,"76":100,"77":101,"78":102,"79":103,"80":104,"81":105,"82":106,"83":107,"84":108,"85":109,"86":110,"87":111,"88":112,"89":113,"90":114,"91":115,"92":116,"93":117,"94":118,"95":119,"96":120,"97":121,"98":122,"99":123,"100":124,"101":125,"102":126,"103":127,"104":128,"105":129,"106":130,"107":131,"108":132,"109":133,"110":134,"111":135,"112":136,"113":137,"114":138,"115":139,"116":140,"117":141,"118":142,"119":143,"120":144,"121":145,"122":146,"123":147,"124":148,"125":149,"126":150,"127":151,"128":152,"129":153,"130":154,"131":155,"132":156,"133":157,"134":158,"135":159,"136":160,"137":161,"138":162,"139":163,"140":164,"141":165,"142":166,"143":167,"144":168,"145":169,"146":170,"147":171,"148":172,"149":173,"150":174,"151":175,"152":176,"153":177,"154":178,"155":179,"156":180,"157":181,"158":182,"159":183,"160":184,"161":185,"162":186,"163":187,"164":188,"16